course: dictionary
lesson: 100
title: Additional: extra, added on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Additional means extra, more than what was there before. The clue is often in the words around it. «The shop charged no additional cost for delivery.» There was no extra charge on top of the price, so additional means extra.
explain: Try the swap check. «You can add additional information on the form.» If you swap in extra, you get «You can add extra information on the form», which still makes sense. So additional means added on to what is already there.
explain: «Additional needs» is an official UK term. It means special educational needs or a disability: extra help a child may need in order to learn. The word still means extra, added on to what most children need. A dictionary can confirm a term like this when the context is not enough.
fact: Additional means extra, more than what was there before.
fact: Additional means added on to something.
fact: «An additional» means one more, on top of the first.
fact: «At no additional cost» means it costs nothing extra.
fact: «Additional needs» (UK) means special educational needs or a disability.
exercise: «The shop charged no additional cost for delivery.» What does additional mean here? | Given back to the customer | Paid early | *Extra, on top of the price | Lower than the price
exercise: «You can add additional information on the form.» What is being added? | Your name only | *Extra information | A pen | A picture of a dog
exercise: Mia says «additional needs» must mean something bad. What does additional mean in this phrase? | Needs for shopping | *Extra needs, on top of what most children need | Broken needs | Needs that are finished
test: «He wrote an additional page for his story.» What does additional mean? | Torn out | *Extra, one more | Very old | Blank
test: Which word is closest in meaning to additional? | Smooth | Early | *Extra | Quiet
exam: Which word is a good swap for additional in «There was an additional charge on the bill»? | Missing | Lost | Smaller | *Extra
